                       '        target_t1_size: Adaptive target size for the T1 '
                       'partition.\n'
                       '\n'
                       '    Algorithm Flow:\n'
                       '        1. Cache lookup (lookup):\n'
                       '           Searches T1 and T2 for block hashes and counts '
                       'consecutive hits\n'
                       '           until a miss or non-ready block is encountered.\n'
                       '\n'
                       '        2. Cache touch (touch) - Adaptive Learning:\n'
                       '           For each key (in reverse order):\n'
                       '           - If in T1: Move to T2 (promotion from recent to '
                       'frequent).\n'
                       '           - If in T2: Move to MRU position (end of queue).\n'
                       '           - If in B1 ghost list: Increase target_t1_size.\n'
                       '           - If in B2 ghost list: Decrease target_t1_size.\n'
                       '\n'
                       '        3. Block eviction (evict) - Adaptive Replacement:\n'
                       '           Determines eviction source based on adaptive '
                       'target:\n'
                       '           - If T1 size >= target_t1_size: Evict from T1, add '
                       'to B1.\n'
                       '           - Otherwise: Evict from T2, add to B2.\n'
                       '           Finally, bound each ghost list size.\n'
                       '\n'
                       '        4. Block insertion (insert):\n'
                       '           New blocks are always inserted into T1 and removed '
                       'from B1/B2 if\n'
                       '           present. Blocks may later be promoted to T2 during '
                       'touch operations.\n'
                       '\n'
                       '    Adaptive Behavior:\n'
                       '        The algorithm self-tunes the recency vs. frequency '
                       'trade-off:\n'
                       '        - B1 hit: Recent access patterns matter more → '
                       'increase T1.\n'
                       '        - B2 hit: Frequent access patterns matter more → '
                       'decrease T1.\n'
                       '    """\n'
                       '\n'
