                             'that position is the\n'
                             '        count at the split.  That is only well defined '
                             'for a grammar of the\n'
                             '        right shape, which is checked here, once, per '
                             'grammar:\n'
                             '\n'
                             '        * reasoning is never re-entered, so there is one '
                             'boundary;\n'
                             '        * every transition out of ``REASONING`` is on a '
                             'token-id terminal\n'
                             '          that resolves in this vocabulary, so the '
                             'boundary is an id and\n'
                             '          not a text position;\n'
                             '        * a transition leaves reasoning exactly when it '
                             'announces\n'
                             '          ``REASONING_END``, so the boundary is the same '
